    33	    /// from the `max_command_sequence_length` gamerule, read when the outermost
    34	    /// execution context is created (`Commands.java:399-403`). Vanilla keeps that
    35	    /// context in a thread-local so nested calls join the ambient chain instead of
    36	    /// getting a fresh quota (`Commands.java:396-414`). A tokio task-local is the
    37	    /// direct analogue here: every nesting level between `execute_function` and the
    38	    /// dispatcher runs on one task through inline `.await`s.
    39	    static REMAINING_COMMAND_QUOTA: Cell<i64>;
    40	}
