codex
A second live gap is confirmed in LongJump: the workspace now has `Navigator::has_pathfinding_malus`, the exact supporting primitive for vanilla `defaultAcceptableLandingSpot`, but the goal still uses a geometry substitute and explicitly documents that as a deviation. I’ll wire the existing navigator into the current candidate predicate, preserving the existing caller and avoiding any new public API.
