The recipe lead is also a genuine server-visible gap: vanilla’s `StonecutterRecipe.display()` emits a dedicated stonecutter display and `recipeBookCategory()` selects the stonecutter category (`StonecutterRecipe.java:37-49`), but the live recipe-book codec only serializes crafting/cooking tables and the registry assigns no stonecutting display IDs. I’m wiring those existing packet/registry call paths, including the dedicated display type/category; this keeps the methods live rather than adding unused model methods.
