   366	        // `TripWireHookBlock.notifyNeighbors` (TripWireHookBlock.java:219-224) calls
   367	        // `updateNeighborsAt` on BOTH the hook and the block it is attached to, with no
   368	        // exclusion. This used to run the `DiodeBlock.updateNeighborsInFront` shape instead
   369	        // (`neighborChanged` on the hook itself, then the attachment block minus one side),
   370	        // which never told the six blocks around the hook that its output had changed - so
   371	        // redstone laid next to a tripwire hook did not react until something else poked it.
   372	        world.update_neighbors(&block_pos, None).await;
   373	        world
   374	            .update_neighbors(&block_pos.offset(direction.opposite().to_offset()), None)
   375	            .await;
